lities for ideal binary gratings as a function of the open fraction. (a) $L=L_{\\lambda}$ (b) $L=0.9L_{\\lambda}$ (c) $L=0.8L_{\\lambda}$. The corresponding classical visibilities are all identical with curve (a).", "label": "fig:idealvisib", "source": "arxiv", "key": "98d49d429a3a64d63c3510ffcece8f6f", "url": "https://inspirehep.net/files/98d49d429a3a64d63c3510ffcece8f6f"}, {"filename": "Fig3.png", "material": "preprint", "caption": "Reduction factor $C_{4}^{\\varepsilon}/C_{4}$, see Eq. (\\ref{eq:F}), of the long-range interaction for dielectric gratings as compared to ideal metals (semi-logarithmic scale). For typical grating materials the static dielectric constant $\\varepsilon\\left( 0\\right) $ is less than 4, leading to a reduction below one half.", "label": "fig:F", "source": "arxiv", "key": "f1056ae179157846c88ed4f590737bb2", "url": "https://inspirehep.net/files/f1056ae179157846c88ed4f590737bb2"}, {"filename": "Fig4.png", "material": "preprint", "caption": "Talbot-Lau visibilities for gratings with a van der Waals interaction as a function of the open fraction. (a) $L=L_{\\lambda}$ (b) $L=0.9L_{\\lambda}$ (c) $L=0.8L_{\\lambda}$. The corresponding classical visibilities are given by the curves (d), (e), (f), respectively.", "label": "fig:C3visib", "source": "arxiv", "key": "f34a53886c92322d36aa7e4ee78818b3", "url": "https://inspirehep.net/files/f34a53886c92322d36aa7e4ee78818b3"}], "inspire_categories": [{"term": "Quantum Physics", "source": "arxiv"}], "preprint_date": "2004-11-18", "author_count": 3, "first_author": {"full_name": "Hornberger, Klaus", "last_name": "Hornberger", "first_name": "Klaus", "recid": 1073918}, "public_notes": [{"source": "arXiv", "value": "20 pages, 4 figures (minor corrections; now in two-column format)"}], "control_number": 2978851, "dois": [{"material": "publication", "source": "arXiv", "value": "10.1103/PhysRevA.70.053608"}], "earliest_date": "2004-11-18", "document_type": ["article"], "texkeys": ["Hornberger:2004thc"], "abstracts": [{"source": "arXiv", "value": "We present a theoretical framework to describe the effects of decoherence on matter waves in Talbot-Lau interferometry. Using a Wigner description of the stationary beam the loss of interference contrast can be calculated in closed form. The formulation includes both the decohering coupling to the environment and the coherent interaction with the grating walls. It facilitates the quantitative distinction of genuine quantum interference from the expectations of classical mechanics. We provide realistic microscopic descriptions of the experimentally relevant interactions in terms of the bulk properties of the particles and show that the treatment is equivalent to solving the corresponding master equation in paraxial approximation.", "abstract_source_suggest": {"input": "arXiv"}}], "primary_arxiv_category": ["quant-ph"], "titles": [{"source": "arXiv", "title": "Theory of decoherence in a matter wave Talbot-Lau interferometer"}], "facet_author_name": ["1979367_J.E. Sipe", "1073918_Klaus Hornberger", "1073935_Markus Arndt"], "_oai": {"sets": ["Literature"], "id": "oai:inspirehep.net:2978851", "updated": "2026-02-09T14:58:12.186955"}, "curated": false, "journal_title_variants": ["Phys.Rev.A", "Phys. Rev. A"], "arxiv_eprints": [{"categories": ["quant-ph"], "value": "quant-ph/0407245"}]}, "updated": "2026-02-09T14:58:12.186955+00:00"}], "total": 1}, "links": {"self": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysreva.70.053608&size=5&page=1", "bibtex": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysreva.70.053608&size=5&page=1&format=bibtex", "latex-eu": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysreva.70.053608&size=5&page=1&format=latex-eu", "latex-us": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysreva.70.053608&size=5&page=1&format=latex-us", "json": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysreva.70.053608&size=5&page=1&format=json", "json-expanded":